1. JavaScript – Definition, Developer, Year, Company & Name History

English Definition:
JavaScript is a high-level programming and scripting language developed by Brendan Eich at Netscape in 1995 to make web pages dynamic and interactive. It was originally developed under the name Mocha, later renamed LiveScript, and finally named JavaScript.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript ek high-level programming aur scripting language hai, jise Brendan Eich ne Netscape company mein 1995 mein develop kiya tha. Iska main purpose web pages ko dynamic aur interactive banana tha. JavaScript ka original naam Mocha tha, baad mein iska naam LiveScript aur finally JavaScript rakha gaya.

Important Points:

Developer: Brendan Eich
Company: Netscape
Year: 1995
Original Name: Mocha
Second Name: LiveScript
Final Name: JavaScript
Main Purpose: Dynamic and Interactive Web Pages
2. JavaScript Version History

English Definition:
JavaScript has evolved through several versions, beginning with the early Netscape versions and later becoming standardized as ECMAScript.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript samay ke saath kai versions mein develop hui. Shuruaati versions Netscape ke browser ke liye aaye, aur baad mein JavaScript ko standardize karne ke liye ECMAScript standard introduce kiya gaya.

5. JavaScript क्यों बनाई गई?

English:
JavaScript was created to add interactivity and dynamic behavior to web pages.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript banane ka main purpose web pages ko static se dynamic banana tha.

Without JavaScript:

Web page mostly sirf information show karta hai.

With JavaScript:

User ke action ke according page response kar sakta hai.

Example:

User → Button Click → JavaScript → Action

Button Click
     ↓
JavaScript Code
     ↓
Message / Calculation / Content Change

6. JavaScript use 

English:
JavaScript is used to create dynamic and interactive web applications.

Hindi:
JavaScript ka use website aur web applications mein different tasks ke liye hota hai.

Main Uses:

1. Form Validation
User ne form mein correct information enter ki hai ya nahi check karna.

2. Events Handling
Click, mouse movement, keyboard press etc. ko handle karna.

3. Dynamic Content
Web page ka content bina page reload kiye change karna.

4. Popup / Alert
Message ya warning show karna.

5. Animation
Web page par animation effects create karna.

6. Calculation
Addition, subtraction, percentage etc. calculate karna.

7. Interactive Websites
Website ko user-friendly aur interactive banana.

8. Web Applications
Gmail, online shopping, dashboards etc. jaise applications develop karne mein use hoti hai.

7. JavaScript और Java में Difference

Important: JavaScript aur Java same language nahi hain.

English:
JavaScript and Java are two different programming languages.

Hindi:
Dono alag-alag programming languages hain. Sirf naam similar hai.

| JavaScript                               | Java                                                      |
| ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| Mainly web development mein use hoti hai | General-purpose/application development mein use hoti hai |
| Scripting/programming language           | Object-oriented programming language                      |
| Browser mein directly run ho sakti hai   | Java Virtual Machine (JVM) par run hoti hai               |
| JavaScript ka standard ECMAScript hai    | Java ka standard Java platform/specifications hain        |

8. JavaScript और ECMAScript

Ye exam mein bahut important hai.

ECMAScript क्या है?

English:
ECMAScript is a standardized specification on which JavaScript is based.

Hindi Explanation:
ECMAScript ek standard/specification hai jo define karta hai ki JavaScript language mein kya rules aur features hone chahiye.

Simple way:

ECMAScript = Standard
JavaScript = ECMAScript ko implement karne wali popular language

Example:

Jaise school mein rules hote hain:

Rules → Standard
Students → Rules follow karte hain

Waise:

ECMAScript → Standard
JavaScript → Standard ko implement karti hai
