JavaScript – Features & Applications
JavaScript  Features
1. Event-Driven-->

English Definition:
JavaScript is an event-driven language that executes code in response to events such as clicking a button, typing a key, or submitting a form.

Example:
Button click → JavaScript function run.

Use: Button click, form submit, mouse movement, keyboard events etc.

2. Prototype-Based

English Definition:
JavaScript is a prototype-based language in which objects can inherit properties and methods from other objects through prototypes.

Easy:
Prototype = Objects ke beech properties/methods share karne ka mechanism.

Use: Object creation aur inheritance ke liye.

3. Cross-Browser

English Definition:
JavaScript is a cross-browser language that can run in major web browsers such as Chrome, Firefox, Edge, and Safari.

Example:
Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari etc.

Use: Aisi website/web application banane ke liye jo different browsers mein work kare.

Note: Browser compatibility ke liye modern web standards aur testing ka dhyan rakhna padta hai.

4. Dynamic Typing

English Definition:
JavaScript is dynamically typed, which means a variable can hold values of different data types during program execution.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript mein variable ka data type pehle se declare karna zaroori nahi hota. Ek hi variable mein alag type ki value store ki ja sakti hai.

let value = 10;
value = "Hello";
value = true;

Yahan value mein pehle number, phir string, phir boolean value store hui.

5. First-Class Functions

English Definition:
In JavaScript, functions are first-class objects, which means functions can be stored in variables, passed as arguments, and returned from other functions.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript mein function ko ek normal value/object ki tarah treat kiya ja sakta hai.

Function ko:

Variable mein store kar sakte hain
Kisi function ko argument ke roop mein de sakte hain
Kisi function se return kar sakte hain
let greet = function() {
    console.log("Hello");
};
6. Closures

Aapne "clusters" likha hai; JavaScript ka relevant feature Closures hai.

English Definition:
A closure is a function that remembers and can access variables from its outer function even after the outer function has finished executing.

Hindi Explanation:
Closure mein inner function apne outer function ke variables ko yaad rakhta hai, chahe outer function ka execution complete ho chuka ho.

Easy:
Closure = Function + uske outer scope ke variables ki memory.

Use: Data privacy, state maintain karne aur callbacks mein.

7. Rich Ecosystem

English Definition:
JavaScript has a rich ecosystem of libraries, frameworks, packages, and tools for developing web, server-side, and mobile applications.

Hindi Explanation:
JavaScript ka ecosystem bahut bada hai. Isme bahut saare libraries, frameworks, packages aur tools available hain jo development ko easy aur fast banate hain.

Examples:
React, Angular, Vue, Express.js, Next.js, React Native etc.

